The Stop prompt requests note-driven spans, current-tree anchor and why validation, removal of only successfully processed notes, and unstaged delivery; the integration guide describes that request separately from the invoked skill. The simplified review-notes skill inspects commits, maintains spans and reports concrete shared-assumption concerns, but does not specify session selection, ID/SHA/document receipt checks or unstaged delivery. Its authority guidance and reconciliation preserve disputed requirements rather than treating committed code as supersession. The real-hook test "emits a fork prompt and allows continuation without another prompt" asserts prompt creation and note-processing phrases for Claude and Codex; it does not establish that the invoked skill follows the prompt or cover OpenCode and Antigravity delivery.
